        "q_products_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between Nasal Strips and Mouth Tape?",
            "answer": "<p>Strips are designed to gently open the nasal passages. Tape is designed to encourage nasal breathing instead of mouth breathing while you sleep. Many people use both together.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q_products_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between the bundles?",
            "answer": "<p>Sleep Bundle comes in three colors — Breathe (Blue), Bold (Red), and Night (Black) — same two products, Strips and Tape, same price either way. The Colour Set includes all three colors of Strips, without Tape. The Season Bundle is a 3-month supply of Black Strips and Black Tape.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q_products_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I buy Strips or Tape on their own?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — both are available individually if you'd rather start with one.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q_products_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Mouth Tape suitable for me?",
            "answer": "<p>Most people adjust within a few nights. If you have a cold, congestion, or any breathing condition, check with a doctor before use.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
